<PageLayout
  title="About Ruta y Ritmo"
  description="A running blog with routes, training, gear, nutrition and health."
  crumb="About"
>
  <p class="lead">
    Ruta y Ritmo is a blog about running: routes, training, gear, nutrition and health.
    A place to read slowly and head out for a run with a clear idea.
  </p>

  <h2>Who writes it</h2>
  <p>Eduard.</p>

  <h2>What you will find</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Routes with distance, elevation gain, terrain and starting point.</li>
    <li>Training explained without personal-best promises.</li>
    <li>Gear: shoes, watches and accessories.</li>
    <li>Nutrition and health with public sources and clear limits.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>A note on the information</h2>
  <p>
    The content is informative and does not replace an individual assessment. If
    something hurts, persists or gets worse, stop and see a professional. Plans are
    starting points, not prescriptions.
  </p>
  <p>
    Routes and practical details are guidance only. Before you set off, check the
    conditions, the track and the available water.
  </p>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>
    Ruta y Ritmo does not accept payment for positive reviews. If there are affiliate
    links or sponsored content, they will be clearly marked. You can read the
    <a href="/en/politica-editorial/">editorial policy</a> and the
    <a href="/en/afiliados/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
